NOTICE

dsh-cadence-standard builds on the DeepSeek Harness ecosystem and references
prior open work:

- The preset structure, the first-turn anchoring mechanism (narrow tool
  surface, expand after the first durable signal) and the agent-visible
  tuning approach reference **yjh051108/dsh-router-standard** (MIT):
  task-aware reasoning-mode router for DeepSeek Harness with three measured
  behavior bands (spec/mixed/react), phase-transition evidence, persona +
  first-turn tool injection, and agent-visible tuning.
- The first-turn anchoring mechanism (zero-tool warm-up turn, narrow first
  request) builds on the bootstrap filter in **xiaobright/dsh-anchored-standard**
  (MIT): two-phase preset with minimal persona + shell/read bootstrap.

